# Tree
guild [test.command.guild, OP]
  <guild: StringArgument> [test.command.guild.guild, OP]
    invite [test.command.guild.invite, OP]
      <players...: PlayerArgument> [test.command.guild.invite.players, OP]
    kick [test.command.guild.kick, OP]
      --silent, -s
      --loud, -l [test.command.guild.kick.option.loud, ALL]
      --reason, -r <reason>
      --by, -b <by>
      <target: PlayerArgument> [test.command.guild.kick.target, OP]

# Permissions
| Permission | Default | Route | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `test.command.guild` | `OP` | `/guild` |  |
| `test.command.guild.guild` | `OP` | `/guild <guild>` |  |
| `test.command.guild.invite` | `OP` | `/guild <guild> invite` |  |
| `test.command.guild.invite.players` | `OP` | `/guild <guild> invite <players...>` |  |
| `test.command.guild.kick` | `OP` | `/guild <guild> kick` |  |
| `test.command.guild.kick.option.loud` | `ALL` | `/guild <guild> kick --loud` |  |
| `test.command.guild.kick.target` | `OP` | `/guild <guild> kick <target>` |  |

# Suggestions of /guild red kick -
--by, --loud, --reason, --silent, -b, -l, -r, -s
# Admin
/guild -> 1
    audit
    Guilds: red
/guild help -> 1
    --------------------------------------------------
    Manage guilds
    Usage:
      /guild <guild> invite <players...>
      /guild <guild> kick <target>
    
    Examples:
      /guild red invite Steve
      /guild red kick -s Steve
    --------------------------------------------------
/guild red invite Steve Alex -> 1
    audit
    Invited Steve, Alex to red
/guild red invite Steve Alex Steve Alex -> RuntimeException: Command syntax error: Incorrect argument for command at position 34: ...lex Steve <--[HERE]
    
/guild red kick Steve -> 1
    audit
    Kicked Steve from red by Admin for ''
/guild red kick Steve -s -> 1
    audit
    Kicked Steve from red by Admin for '' silently
/guild red kick -s -l Steve -> RuntimeException: Command syntax error: Incorrect argument for command at position 21: ...ick -s -l <--[HERE]
    
/guild red kick -r spam Steve -> 0
    --reason requires --by.
/guild red kick -r spam -b Alex Steve -l -> 1
    audit
    Kicked Steve from red by Alex for 'spam' loudly
